---
import "@styles/global.module.css";
import Header from "@components/header.astro";
import Footer from "@components/footer.astro";
import Meta from "@components/meta.astro";
import Cursor from "@components/cursor.astro";
import Scripts from "@components/scripts.astro";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <Meta name="Updating usernames on all social platforms" description="I am updating usernames on all platforms, and here's why" />
        <Scripts />
        <Cursor />
    </head>

    <body>
        <canvas id="background"></canvas>
        <!-- God damnit, I'm forced to use inline styles because Astro is stupid -->
        <div style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;">
            <Header />
            <main>
                <h1>I am updating usernames on all platforms, here's why</h1>
                
                <p>it all started with mldkyt, and it seemed like I would have my username forever. that's not the case anymore.</p>

                <p>previously, I've already tried many times to find a new name for myself. chatgpt, username generators... anything! but I am not a creative person, and a task like this isn't really easy for me. (same goes for my profile picture on everything, if I didn't need a pfp everywhere, I wouldn't set one)</p>

                <p>for a while (around March 2024 to September 2024) I used to be Akatsuki, and even registered my Nekoweb account under that username. But later, I decided that Akatsuki isn't really a good name for me and returned to mldkyt. Later I took the Japanese name suffix "chan" and replaced the end of my shortened username "mld" with chan so "mldchan" came out.</p>

                <p>under this "new" username I renamed pretty much everything, and even registered <a href="https://lunya.pet">mldchan.dev</a>. but I am bored of this username now.</p>

                <p>as I figured out back in 2023 (Specifically around August-September 2023) that I am transgender, and that I would love to live as a girl, a new challenge was with it. i should find myself a name. like not a new username, a new name, like for a person. it took me a pretty long time to figure that out (about 1.5 years!) but I finally settled on Luna (<i>now which Luna?</i>). there were many iterations of this, there was "Emily", created from how "mld" sounded. with this I also modified the name slightly and added a "nya" (a cat sound) into it, resulting with "Lunya".</p>

                <p>with this, I started registering any new social accounts under that new name, and frequently started updating any existing profiles from the name "mldchan" or "mldkyt" to "Lunya", "LunyaUwU", "lunya.pet" or anything similar. I registered the domain <a href="https://lunya.pet">lunya.pet</a> which hosts my website and almost all of my services. I migrated a lot of them over.</p>

                <p>for instance, <a href="https://social.mldchan.dev/">social.mldchan.dev</a> &rarr; <a href="https://fedi.lunya.pet/">fedi.lunya.pet</a>, <a href="https://code.mldchan.dev/">code.mldchan.dev</a> &rarr; <a href="https://git.lunya.pet">git.lunya.pet</a>, the list goes on.</p>

                <h2>what's gonna happen to mldchan.dev now?</h2>           

                <p>probably will let it expire, or will continue hosting things on this and redirecting users from it. i am planning to make the main website a redirect with a form to report any forgotten links to the new domain.</p>

                <p>unlikely that I'll let it expire and will extend it for another year tho.</p>

                <p>if you want to ask me any questions regarding this username change, feel free to <a href="/discord">join my Discord server</a>.</p>
            </main>
            <Footer />
        </div>
        <script is:inline defer src="/scripts/background.js"></script>
    </body>
</html>
